// main.cla: internal/lowlevel's TestRtInc/ToolboxIncludeFallback fixture
// (binary-files phase Task 7). This file has no toolbox/ sibling of its
// own, so `include "toolbox/files.cla"` only resolves via the
// rtdir-sibling fallback (spec section 3.5). The `window` decl
// independently pulls in runtime/clarus/uidialogs.cla, which itself
// `include`s "../../toolbox/files.cla" -- proving the fallback-resolved
// copy of files.cla and the runtime module's relatively-resolved copy
// dedup to the same identity (same incKey) instead of double-parsing/
// redeclaring.
//
// `include "sub/foo.cla"` (fix round 1, review finding) adds a NESTED
// includer spelling ITS OWN fallback target "../toolbox/osutils.cla"
// (one climb fewer than a top-level "toolbox/x.cla" spelling, since
// foo.cla sits one directory deeper) -- both spellings must normalize to
// the same key and resolve via the identical fallback join. Deliberately
// targets a DIFFERENT toolbox file (osutils.cla, not files.cla) than
// this file's own direct include: `expand()`'s dedup marks a path as
// "seen" even on a FAILED attempt (drive.cla:940-947), so a nested
// include normalizing to the SAME bare path as an already-attempted
// direct include would short-circuit through dedup before ever reaching
// the fallback -- masking, not exercising, the fix under review. See
// sub/foo.cla's own header comment.
include "toolbox/files.cla"
include "sub/foo.cla"

window Main {
    title: "probe"
    size: 200, 100
}
